# System Admin Portal (§13.5, tier-0) — HQ-side configuration.

# Where this portal reaches a Centre Edge in dev (proxied under /api/*).
# In production the HQ WireGuard link carries this; never a public URL.
EDGE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4000

# ── THE decryption key (HSM stand-in) ───────────────────────────────────
# The RSA private half matching the Edge's SYSTEM_ADMIN_PUBLIC_KEY_PEM. This is
# the ONLY place in the whole system where a private key exists — a centre never
# holds one, which is what makes a fully compromised centre yield ciphertext
# (INV-6). In production this variable does not exist at all: the unwrap is an
# HSM operation and the key is unextractable.
#
# For development, generate the pair once (idempotent — safe to re-run):
#     node ../hq-demo-key/ensure-keys.mjs
# then point at the private half. Prefer the _FILE form: a PKCS#8 PEM is
# multi-line and does not survive a plain .env value intact.
HQ_PRIVATE_KEY_PEM_FILE=../hq-demo-key/hq-demo-private.pem

# Inline alternative, if you must (literal \n escapes are accepted):
# HQ_PRIVATE_KEY_PEM=
